{
  "_comment": [
    "Free-text `world_fold.rs:N` references the digest gate does not own.",
    "This list is a RATCHET: verify_world_fold_citations.py fails when a",
    "module cites a line number that is not in its list here, so the set can",
    "only shrink.  Cite `world_fold.rs::<item_name>` instead -- an item name",
    "does not move when a line is inserted above it, and the `lines=`/sha256",
    "marker still owns the exact range it hashes.",
    "Every entry below is a reference that could not be resolved to one item",
    "with total confidence; the reason for each is recorded in",
    "extractor/native/runs/prose_refs/residue.tsv.",
    "The budget is per (module, line number), not per site: deleting one entry's",
    "occurrence and citing the SAME number again elsewhere in the SAME module is",
    "not caught. Binding an entry to a position would mean recording a line number",
    "in a file whose own line numbers move, which is the failure this check exists",
    "to stop, and the hole admits no number the module was not already allowed."
  ],
