  "_documents_comment": [
    "Free-text `world_fold.rs:N` references in the design documents.",
    "Same RATCHET as `modules` above, and for a sharper reason: a module's",
    "stale line number sits beside a digest-gated marker a reader can fall",
    "back on, a document's does not.  Nothing compiles prose, and the only",
    "reader of one of these is a human who opens world_fold.rs at that line",
    "and believes what is there.",
    "This is the baseline taken when the document check was added; it was",
    "NOT verified line by line against world_fold.rs, because doing so",
    "resolves against a file that is being edited.  Every entry is a",
    "reference to CONVERT to `world_fold.rs::<item_name>`, not one that has",
    "been checked and blessed.  Adding a NEW number here needs a reason."
  ],
